Plan: Restructure ANTIK-HOLZ for Multi-Product CMS Integration
📋 Overview
Transform the monolithic ANTIK-HOLZ order form into a scalable, CMS-driven multi-product platform while maintaining the light minimalistic design system defined in CLAUDE.md. Current State: 1356-line monolithic React component with hardcoded product data Target State: Modular component architecture with CMS-managed product catalog supporting multiple product types (Deski, Belki, Panele ścienne, Płyty meblowe, Deski podłogowe)
🎯 Goals
Enable CMS-driven product management - no code deploys for catalog changes
Support multiple product types with shared UI components
Maintain design consistency via CLAUDE.md style guide across all products
Preserve existing functionality - zero breaking changes during migration
Enable future scaling - easy to add new products, pricing models, form fields
Two separate views:
Customer View (Frontend) - order form for end customers
Admin View (Dashboard) - order management and catalog editing for business owner
No payment integration - orders submitted via email/form only (payment handling later)
🏗️ Technology Stack Selection
Backend & CMS: Strapi 4.x ✅
Why Strapi:
✅ Headless CMS with powerful content modeling
✅ Built-in REST & GraphQL APIs
✅ Polish admin panel UI (important for non-technical users)
✅ Media library for product images
✅ Role-based permissions for catalog management
✅ Easy local development + deployment
✅ PostgreSQL support for production reliability
Alternatives considered:
❌ Payload CMS - too developer-focused, steeper learning curve
❌ Custom API - too much development time, reinventing the wheel
❌ Contentful/Sanity - paid services, vendor lock-in
Database: PostgreSQL ✅
Why PostgreSQL:
✅ Reliable relational model for structured product data
✅ JSONB support for flexible product configurations
✅ Free and open-source
✅ Excellent Strapi integration
Frontend State Management: TanStack Query (React Query) ✅
Why TanStack Query:
✅ Perfect for fetching/caching CMS data
✅ Built-in loading/error states
✅ Automatic background refetching
✅ Minimal boilerplate vs Redux
✅ Works great with REST APIs
Alternatives considered:
❌ Redux/Zustand - overkill for read-heavy catalog data
❌ Context API only - no caching, poor performance
Form Management: React Hook Form + Zod ✅
Why React Hook Form + Zod:
✅ Better performance than current manual state management
✅ Zod provides type-safe validation schemas
✅ Easy to make forms dynamic based on product config
✅ Minimal re-renders
Styling: TailwindCSS 3.x (keep current) ✅
